In the testcase, the method `IndexOf(x)` is called on the array list. Three conditions are assumed that the return value can be negative if the array list does not contain the element `x`, and the `Contains(x)` method should return `false` for this condition.

In addition, it considers that when `IndexOf(x)` returns a negative value, the count of the array list should remain the same. To verify the count increment, `AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount - 1);` is used.

